        <definition>unsigned llvm::BasicBlockInfo::Offset</definition>
        <argsstring></argsstring>
        <name>Offset</name>
        <qualifiedname>llvm::BasicBlockInfo::Offset</qualifiedname>
        <initializer>= 0</initializer>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Offset - Distance from the beginning of the function to the beginning of this basic block. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Offsets are computed assuming worst case padding before an aligned block. This means that subtracting basic block offsets always gives a conservative estimate of the real distance which may be smaller.</para>
<para>Because worst case padding is used, the computed offset of an aligned block may not actually be aligned. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
